From 3930745d8593bb9dffb3d0755affcdefb37585e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 21:44:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tests/fuzz: fix out-of-bounds read in header validation
 harness

_ubus_validate_hdr() passed the input straight to ubus_validate_hdr()
whenever size was not greater than sizeof(struct ubus_msghdr). That
condition is backwards and too small: ubus_validate_hdr() dereferences
the struct blob_attr located immediately after the header, so the
harness needs at least sizeof(ubus_msghdr) + sizeof(blob_attr) bytes.
An 8-byte input (exactly the header size) reached the validator and
read blob_raw_len() one blob_attr past the end of the buffer.

Require the full header plus the trailing blob_attr before validating.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 tests/fuzz/test-fuzz.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tests/fuzz/test-fuzz.c b/tests/fuzz/test-fuzz.c
index 7a7a1eb..6001b08 100644
--- a/tests/fuzz/test-fuzz.c
+++ b/tests/fuzz/test-fuzz.c
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
 
 static void _ubus_validate_hdr(const uint8_t *data, size_t size)
 {
-	if (size > sizeof(struct ubus_msghdr))
+	if (size < sizeof(struct ubus_msghdr) + sizeof(struct blob_attr))
 		return;
 
 	ubus_validate_hdr((struct ubus_msghdr *) data);
